module gunbc.guarantee_stall.argument_shape_undecided_at_a_declared_position_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { OutsideTheLadder, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, ClimbableButUnbuilt, BoundedPopulation, climbs_when }

data argument_shape_undecided_at_a_declared_position_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "a decidable argument-shape mismatch is accepted with no diagnostic at a declared position: an unapplied nullary function stands where a value of its return type is declared, and a String stands at a generic formal — both measured accepted in the same compile in which a String at a CONCRETE position is refused, so refusal is reachable at that position and the deferral is a gap rather than a limit",
  current: OutsideTheLadder,
  ceiling: StructurallyImpossible,
  blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
  population: BoundedPopulation { members: ["v1.compiler.infer", "test.claim.argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test"] },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "TWO TRIGGERS AT DIFFERENT GRAINS, BOTH NAMED, because this class is below its ceiling for two independent reasons and section 4b(2) forbids leaving either implicit. (1) THE CLASS TRIGGER: the declared-type judgment decides argument shape from the ARGUMENT'S OWN CONSTRUCTOR before consulting the declared position -- function-type against non-function-type, and primitive against constructed -- sufficient that an_unapplied_function_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused and a_string_at_a_generic_position_is_refused both reach a located, typed refusal in the same run in which a_string_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused already does; on that day both rows flip to permanent regression controls per DESIGN 4b(4), which is this stall's stated end rather than an implied one. (2) THE EVIDENCE TRIGGER, WHICH IS SEPARATE AND IS THE ONE BLOCKING TODAY: test.claim.argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test is admitted to v2.workflow.required_floor required_gate_prefixes, sufficient that a required lane RUNS these four rows rather than suppressing them as dormant. The probe matches no prefix today, so the floor discovers and does not run it, and an expected-red enrolment was REMOVED rather than kept because floor_expected_red asserts that an enrolled identity reaches its subject and answers. Until that admission the class is PROVEN BUT UNROUTED: it executes, it discriminates, and no required lane consumes it, so this row's rung rests on a human-run claim_batch invocation. THE CONDITION ON ASKING, stated so that NOT TODAY does not decay into NEVER: the admission is requested when the runner pool is not saturated, and as its OWN change rather than as a rider on a repair -- it adds four rows to every required floor run, and it was deferred on a day when the pool sat at roughly twenty concurrent runs and main had gone red on memory pressure from that load. The blocker is ClimbableButUnbuilt on both triggers: neither is waiting on a grounding that does not exist.")
}
